                  "coverage": "One image of the photosphere reconstructed with the public SQUEEZE code from 909 squared visibilities and 603 closure phases measured by VLTI/PIONIER on four nights of September 2014 in the H band (1.62-1.73 micrometres, three channels), convolved to the 2.1 milliarcsecond interferometric beam and cast onto a sphere of the radius the disc and the Gaia parallax imply. The camera is computed: the star has no measured rotation axis, so the display axis is celestial north in the plane of the sky, the display meridian is the sub-Earth point at the epoch, and the pixel scale is the reconstruction's. Nothing finer than the beam is shown. The colours are a legend for reconstructed relative intensity in one infrared band, not colour or temperature. The far hemisphere is unobserved."
